:: Carter House Intro Part 1 [nobr]

/* Intro */
You walk up to the house that matches <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span>’s description. A blue house with a red mailbox. It also helps that it has the name <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Kent”</span> painted onto the mailbox. This has to be the place. You walk up and knock on the red door, waiting a brief moment before knocking again when you get no response. <span style="Color:Yellow">Silence.</span> Looking at the window, you don’t notice any inside lights on. Strange, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> didn’t mention anytime he wouldn’t be available today. <span style="Color:Yellow">This has to be the right house, so you wonder where they could have gone?</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Frown",
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I got it!”</span> You jump as you hear the familiar voice of <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> coming, not from inside the house, but around back. You walk over to the side gate and realize that it is open with a dark blue truck parked up near it, it’s tailgate open. You peek into the backyard and see a suspiciously <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span>-shaped shadow waving his arms about as you hear the boy again. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Will this nail work? Here you go!”</span> You hear other voices too, but <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span>’s is so loud and recognizable it is the only one that you can make out. <br>
<br>
You clear your throat and call out his name, feeling a little too awkward to just walk into his backyard without invitation. You hear a noise of realization <span style="Color:LightGreen">and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> jumps out from behind the house a moment later, wearing his trunks and a t-shirt.</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Frown",
            },
        },
        {
            Name: "Carter",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Swim Shirt",
                Mouth: "Frown",
                Blush: 1,
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$CarterNickname</span>!?”</span> He says, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Shoot, were you waiting out there? I thought I could hear the doorbell from here. Sorry about that!”</span> You chuckle nervously, realizing you didn’t even consider looking for a doorbell, and are waved over by the boy as he rushes out of sight again. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Could you shine the light over here please.”</span> You hear the familiar, yet muffled, voice of <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span>’s father say as you turn the corner to see <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> standing over two people lying under the back patio. You then hear a drill go off for a second before <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span>, holding a box of nails, asks his father if he needs another one. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Nah, should be good now. Can you and your friend walk on it a minute, so I can make sure it’s sturdy?”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> nods, placing the box down on the deckchair before grabbing you by the hand and climbing onto the patio. You both stand on the new, unpainted board, stomping and jumping around as you hear his father make noises of confirmation down below. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Nice, not even a budge! That should do it!”</span> His father laughs. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“That’s good, don’t want someone falling through that and breaking their ankle.”</span> A young, yet mature voice laughs, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“And by someone, I mean our walking tornado.”</span> A teen who looks about a year older than Gabe slides out from under the patio, standing up and giving <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> a sly wink. <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Smirk",
            },
        },
        {
            Name: "Carter",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Swim Shirt",
                Mouth: "Frown",
                Eyes: "Tired",
                Blush: 1,
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I am not a walking tornado!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> protests, puffing out his cheeks, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I don’t even have wind powers!”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“It’s an expression, ‘Ultraboy’.”</span> He laughs, before turning to you. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Hey, I’m <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span>, this terror’s big brother. You’re <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$CarterNickname</span>, right? Pleasure to meet you.”</span> He wipes his hands on his shirt to get the dust off before giving you a firm handshake. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span> speaks in a very polite tone, and it is only as he stands before you that you realize how large his frame is. He, much like his father, clearly takes physical ability seriously. <span style="Color:LightGreen">You quickly wonder how <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> is so weak and scrawny when every other man in his family is so strong. You remember <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span>’s twin and start to imagine him as a buff version of <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span>, chuckling to yourself.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“So, dad, you’re going to open the pool now, right?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> asks, bouncing up and down excitedly. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Yeah, yeah.”</span> His father laughs, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You’ve earned your reward. I have to get this painted before your mom gets home anyway, so I’ll be out here to keep an eye on you boys. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span>, have time to help me take the cover off before you leave?”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Yeah,”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span> pulls out and checks his phone, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Megan</span> hasn’t messaged that she’s on her way yet, so I should have time.”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Thanks.”</span> His dad claps the dust off his hands before patting you and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> on the shoulder. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Why don’t you show your friend around while we get this done? You wouldn’t want to be a bad host.”</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
        {
            Name: "Carter",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Swim Shirt",
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You’re right!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> jumps up, a sparkle in his eye, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$CarterNickname</span>, go back to the front door and ring the bell. I’ll greet you properly!”</span> All three of you chuckle at <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span>’s enthusiasm as you are shooed back down the side gate to the front door. <span style="Color:LightGreen">Seems <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span>’s energy is the same at home.</span> <br>
<br>

<<linkreplace"Continue">>
    The instant you ring the doorbell, the door flies open. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Hey, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$Player.Name</span>! Welcome to the Kent abode!”</span> He does a little bow like the ones butler’s do in movies that causes you both to chuckle. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Come on in!”</span> You walk into the large living room, taken up mostly by a large couch that looks like it can seat about 10 people. <span style="Color:Yellow">Then your eyes fall on the TV mounted on the wall, massive and shining! It looks about double the size of the one you have at home and you instinctively take a step back, worried it may fall and crush you.</span> Your awe must have been obvious as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> laughs. <br>

        <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Happy",
                },
            },
            {
                Name: "Carter",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Swim Shirt",
                    Mouth: "Happy",
                },
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Yeah, Dad and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span> are SUPER into sports and stuff. He spent his entire bonus on that last Christmas. Mom only complained about it until he pointed out she can watch her broadcasts on there. She likes to ‘critique herself’, whatever that means.”</span> He shrugs, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’m not allowed to touch it. But it’s cool since they put the old TV in my room! It’s super cool, but a little smaller! That’s probably a good thing though, I don’t think this would fit in my room. Oh, but they let me watch wrestling and cartoons on it over the weekend!”</span> You nod along; eyes locked on the massive TV as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> leads you further into the house. <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Living room is the main room. Kitchen and stuff are that way, that’s how you get to the yard. Bathroom over here. Oh, and the best room is over here!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> grabs your hand and leads you over to a blue door with letters pinned to the front in different colors along with a colored pencil drawing of what you can only describe as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> dressed like Ultraman. <span style="Color:Pink">It is super cute, even if it’s a little childish for his age.</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Ta-da!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> swings the door open with flair, welcoming you to his bedroom. It has blue walls, as expected, and is about the size of your own room. His closet lines the wall to his left while immediately to the right of the door is his bed, a twin-sized bed with the expected Ultraman sheets and blanket on it. It is partially made, like it was done in a hurry, and its odd placement so close to the door confuses you for a moment until you see the rest of the room. <br>
    <br>
    Across from the bed is his dresser, keeping all the ‘essential’ parts of his bedroom crammed to one side. This leaves the remainder of his room quite open, with his bed acting like a pseudo wall. Past his bed is an open space surrounded by shelves, bookcases, and a large toybox. Two beanbags sit against his bed, facing the opposite wall with a television set. It sits on an entertainment stand bursting with movies and DVD boxsets of animated shows, most of them superhero themed. An older video game system sits tucked between some of them as well. <br>
    <br>
    Next to the window to the left of the TV is a bookshelf also bursting with stuff, though these appear to be mostly comics and a few books. You also see some DVDs that didn’t fit onto the stand jammed in here as well. <span style="Color:LightGreen">The best way you could describe it is an organized mess. It looks cluttered, though there seems to be a method to the chaos.</span> <br>
    <br>
    Though the final shelf stands out, sitting right next to his bed. Unlike the cluttered, overflowing shelves of the others, this one seems neat, organized, and displayed with purpose. Figures standing proud in posed scenes, comics neatly placed inside plastic, a few signed photos of <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> from various ages with actors and writers he’s met at conventions with their signatures. This must be where <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> keeps his prized possessions, made even more obvious by the bottom two shelves, locked behind sliding glass where he keeps his most precious things. <br>
    <br>
    You lean down to inspect the bottoms shelves as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> watches anxiously, wondering what you think of his room. You notice him tidy up a few things and kick a duct taped box and some toy handcuffs under his bed. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Yeah, I keep the important stuff in there. Dad keeps the key, or I’d show you. But if you lie down on your stomach, it’s pretty cool to look at.”</span> <span style="Color:Pink">You notice <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span>’s blush and can just imagine him spending hours lying and staring at these.</span> <br>
    <br>
    In a second layer glass case in the center is a comic book on a stand. You guess it must be expensive, since it’s sealed twice. It’s an old Ultraman comic, showing a very early design of Ultraman looking like he is about to hit someone with a green car. Strange. Next to that are some framed photos, one of <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> with a very old gentleman. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> looks about 5 and looks like he’s sitting on Santa’s lap, but instead it’s a very old man holding up an ink pen. Said pen, or at least one that looks just like it, sits on a stand in front of the photo. You make a note to ask <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> about what all these things mean at a later date. <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color:Yellow">One thing that stands out is a photo placed faced down in the corner.</span> You wonder if maybe if fell and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> hadn’t noticed, but something about it looks intentional. You stand back up, smiling and complimenting <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span>’s collection. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> smiles widely at this, his worries evaporating at your praise. <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Thanks! <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span> says I’m a bit of a hoarder, but he just doesn’t understand that these are collectables!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> laughs, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Don’t tell anyone, but some of this stuff is worth – like – a LOT of money! Dad says I shouldn’t blurt that out, but I trust you.”</span> <span style="Color:LightGreen">He smiles as you take one last look around the room. It’s cluttered, but it just screams <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span>.</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> is in the middle of pointing out one of his collectables when his father calls <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Pool’s ready! Come on out!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> smiles widely at this, dashing to his window and peeking out into the yard. <br>

        <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Happy",
                },
            },
            {
                Name: "Carter",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Swim",
                    Mouth: "Happy",
                },
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oooohhh! Heck yeah!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> <span style="Color:Pink">jumps with joy before quickly yanking off his shirt,</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You can get changed in here if you need to. I’ll wait outside. Our pool is so cool, we have a slide and a jumping board and it has these jets that make it all bubbly and stuff! It’s way more fun than the one at school, since we can play around! We haven’t been able to use it for the last few months since they had to replace a bunch of stuff. I’m so excited!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> <span style="Color:Pink">jumps with joy, now wearing just his Ultraman trunks, which seem a tiny bit too big, like most of <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span>’s clothes, and dangle down just enough to look adorable on his tiny body.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’ll meet you outside!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span> dashes out, leaving you alone in his room to get changed to swim. <br>
    <br>
    It’s a little awkward to be alone in <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter </span>’s bedroom. You think about maybe snooping around <span style="Color:Yellow">but figure you should just get changed since he’s waiting for you.</span> <br>
